+      "title": "Draft: exact KPZ balances can coexist with unequal exponent thresholds",
+      "statement": "DRAFT, independent review pending. For integers n>=2, let a_n=1/4 on even n and 1/3 on odd n. Set X_n=n^(a_n) Z for a symmetric random sign Z, and D_n=n^((1+a_n)/2). Define chi_a as the infimum of q with some alpha>0 such that sup_n E exp(alpha |X_n|/n^q)<infinity; define chi_b as the supremum of q with some N such that inf_{n>=N} Var(X_n)/n^(2q)>0. Define xi_a and xi_b in the same way using D_n for upper moments and E D_n for lower bounds. Then chi_a=1/3, chi_b=1/4, xi_a=2/3, xi_b=5/8. At every scale sqrt(Var(X_n))=D_n^2/n; both endpoint identities chi_a=2xi_a-1 and chi_b=2xi_b-1 hold, but the threshold gaps are 1/12 and 1/24. This refutes an abstract inference from scale balances to common strong exponents. These observables are NOT an iid FPP model; no FPP nonexistence or exponent theorem follows.",
