+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Draft: changing a coupling cannot erase a raw linear FPP drift gap",
+      "statement": "DRAFT, independent review pending. Suppose U_n/n has almost-sure limsup at most mu-c under its marginal sequence law, while V_n/n tends almost surely to mu under its marginal sequence law, for a deterministic c>0. Under any joint coupling at each n and any 0<epsilon<c/2, P((V_n-U_n)/n>=c-2epsilon) is at least 1-P(U_n/n>mu-c+epsilon)-P(V_n/n<mu-epsilon), and this tends to 1. No independence is required, and the coupling may vary with n. In bounded positive nondegenerate iid FPP, w375's audited connector-separated detour construction supplies this drift gap between unrestricted and directed axial passage times. For the Uniform[1,2] low=[1,5/4], high=[7/4,2], k=6 witness, the certified saving is at least 1/3758096384. A different coupling alone therefore cannot give a raw o_P(n) approximation. This does not exclude different deterministic centering or equality of centered fluctuation universality classes. The mathematical argument and exact input assumptions are in w376 ATTEMPT.md and PEER_AUDIT.md; novelty and target solution are not claimed.",
