+      "title": "Draft: P0110 law certificates must verify exponent existence",
+      "statement": "DRAFT source-audit guidance, independent review pending. P0110 asks for a nondegenerate iid undirected lattice FPP law with well-defined fluctuation and wandering exponents satisfying chi=2xi-1; equation (4.19) and Question 22 of Auffinger-Damron-Hanson, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1511.03262, do not settle exponent existence or mandate only one definition. A proposed solution must state its exponent definition and prove existence for the exhibited law. If it uses Chatterjee Theorem 1.1, https://annals.math.princeton.edu/wp-content/uploads/annals-v177-n2-p07-p.pdf, it must check iid nearest-neighbor weights on Z^d, d>=2, a nearly-gamma law, finite moment generating function near zero, the uniform upper exponential-moment and tail-uniform lower variance/mean-deviation premises, and chi_a=chi_b plus xi_a=xi_b. A scale balance or conditional theorem citation alone supplies none of the two coincidence certificates. Keep tail cutoffs and all-endpoint infima distinct. Directed-model transfers must account for deterministic centering and an error on the fluctuation scale; changing the coupling alone cannot erase separated raw marginal drifts. Current openness is UNKNOWN; this draft certifies no solved target or novelty.",
